{
    "background_story": "Rudy was a gentle giant, a terrestrial tortoise who roamed the arid deserts of the American Southwest. For decades, he slowly traversed the sandy dunes, his shell a testament to his age and wisdom. Rudy's home was the dry, cracked earth, where he would often burrow into the soil to escape the scorching sun. Despite his slow pace, he had a deep understanding of the land, knowing the best spots to find succulent cacti and refreshing oases. Rudy's terrestrial nature made him a master of adaptation, able to survive in one of the harshest environments on Earth. As the years passed, he became a local legend, with many a desert traveler seeking out the wise and venerable Rudy, who seemed to embody the spirit of the desert itself.",
